1
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:05,100
=The Truth (Season 4)=
(New bonus scenes)

2
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:07,260
(The crew has fun
picking their ID cards)

3
00:00:07,860 --> 00:00:09,710
(Thunder, the Supreme Phantom Dragonlord)
Employee ID.

4
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:12,910
Thunder, the Supreme Phantom Dragonlord.

5
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:13,630
Thunder?

6
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:14,980
(Now that's a thunderous name)

7
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:18,550
Princess Purrdoodle.

8
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:19,470
No, you have to say it

9
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:20,940
like you're calling out
an ultimate move.

10
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:21,820
(Channeling mysterious powers)

11
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:26,030
Lanalan Lunalan Genius Boy.

12
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:26,790
Isn't that you?

13
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:28,390
I'm the genius boy.

14
00:00:28,660 --> 00:00:29,940
(Claiming the genius boy title)

15
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:30,750
Obviously that's me.

16
00:00:31,380 --> 00:00:32,420
(Fine, since you're younger)

17
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:34,230
Leggy McShy,

18
00:00:34,230 --> 00:00:34,860
King of...

19
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:35,480
What?

20
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:36,680
King of Awkward.

21
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:37,220
(That one's a mouthful)

22
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:38,580
Innocent...

23
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:40,600
Innocent Hunk.

24
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:42,140
(Zero hesitation)
Long-legged, innocent pretty boy.

25
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:43,060
(Yep, that's me)

26
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:45,060
(Back to clue hunting)

27
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:46,710
This one's me.

28
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:51,590
Princess Donasia Ronaswa Ulala.

29
00:00:54,080 --> 00:00:55,550
(Battle of the princesses)
Am I really not the princess?

30
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:56,830
(Keeping everyone happy)
Two leads. Two princesses.

31
00:00:56,840 --> 00:00:58,350
Fake princess.

32
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:00,660
(Don't care)

33
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:02,100
(If I wear it, it's mine)

34
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:05,670
Proudblood, Ruthless Duke, Mad Dragon.

35
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:06,390
That sounds like you.

36
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:07,390
Why me?

37
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:08,350
Mad Dragon?

38
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:10,790
You even look like a Digimon today.

39
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:11,710
Yeah, okay.

40
00:01:13,490 --> 00:01:15,620
Proudblood, Ruthless Duke, Mad Dragon.

41
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:16,430
(Ning doesn't get it)
Why me?

42
00:01:16,430 --> 00:01:17,260
You're Mad Dragon.

43
00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:18,350
You're definitely Mad Dragon.

44
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:19,350
I'm a dinosaur.

45
00:01:19,360 --> 00:01:21,470
(Dino or dragon?)
Mad Dragon, dinosaur... I'm the dino.

46
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:24,750
There are a few. You can choose.

47
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:26,630
What does choosing one do?

48
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:27,710
I'm telling you,

49
00:01:27,710 --> 00:01:29,260
what you pick could really matter.

50
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:29,710
I think so too.

51
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:31,270
Maybe a later clue will decide

52
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:32,990
(Wild guess)
whoever has this card is the killer.

53
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,070
Just like that?

54
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:35,350
Could be.

55
00:01:35,350 --> 00:01:35,940
(Scheming...)

56
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:37,550
Then you take this princess one.

57
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:41,150
(Crowning the princess)
You get Princess Purrdoodle.

58
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:42,350
Why do we have to claim these?

59
00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:43,270
I don't want one.

60
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:44,390
(Starting to sweat)
I... This isn't ours.

61
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:46,150
Why do we have to claim these things?

62
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:47,890
They really suit you guys.

63
00:01:47,890 --> 00:01:48,530
(Ke has a thought)
Okay.

64
00:01:48,530 --> 00:01:49,200
We don't have to claim them.

65
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:50,470
We can hold onto them for now.

66
00:01:50,470 --> 00:01:51,430
Keep them as evidence.

67
00:01:51,430 --> 00:01:52,100
Right?

68
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:52,580
Okay.

69
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:53,990
(Here, you take it)
You keep it.

70
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,750
Can you read the Leggy McShy ID again?

71
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:04,790
(King of Awkward)
Leggy McShy, King of Awkward,

72
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:06,630
Innocent Hunk.

73
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:07,710
Look closely at that word.

74
00:02:08,180 --> 00:02:08,540
(Kinda)

75
00:02:08,540 --> 00:02:09,860
(Leaning in for a look)

76
00:02:10,540 --> 00:02:12,300
Kinda Awkward.

77
00:02:15,050 --> 00:02:15,890
King of...

78
00:02:15,890 --> 00:02:17,090
(Now it makes sense)
Oh, Kinda Awkward.

79
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:19,350
(Jin is confused)
Why did we all read it as "King of"?

80
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:21,270
Because it looks closed off.

81
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:23,990
King of Awkward.

82
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:25,660
(Still stuck on it)
A room full of awkward people,

83
00:02:25,660 --> 00:02:26,650
and now their king too.

84
00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:28,780
(That got him)
King of Awkward.

85
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:33,060
(Picking employee IDs)

86
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:37,470
I want to give him this one.

87
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:39,510
This one's for you.

88
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:41,670
I want to be...

89
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:42,310
Which one do you want?

90
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:43,710
I don't want this.

91
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:45,110
Because if you take this one,

92
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:46,150
you'll have to play a little princess.

93
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:47,590
I want to be Mad Dragon.

94
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,510
Then I take Princess Purrdoodle.

95
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:50,830
Or... yours.

96
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:51,830
That princess one.

97
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:52,810
You take this.

98
00:02:52,810 --> 00:02:53,930
This one's too hard to remember.

99
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:55,470
Never mind.

100
00:02:55,920 --> 00:02:57,350
Ning, how about you take this one?

101
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:58,790
Princess Ulala?

102
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:00,910
No way. What if...

103
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:02,510
(Ning senses danger)
What if he makes me kiss him?

104
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:03,380
What am I supposed to do?

105
00:03:03,380 --> 00:03:04,390
You were a bridesmaid last episode.

106
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:05,630
What won't you do at this point?

107
00:03:05,640 --> 00:03:06,910
And I'm guessing something

108
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:07,590
will happen later,

109
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:10,150
since we're pretending
to be new employees.

110
00:03:10,150 --> 00:03:10,650
Right.

111
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:14,950
What if each card sends us down
a different route?

112
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:15,710
Don't worry about that.

113
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:16,670
That's definitely possible.

114
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:18,500
(Seriously?)

115
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:20,430
The first thing new employees do

116
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:22,550
is go through security
with the Group Leader and Team Leader

117
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:23,390
for a full inspection.

118
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:24,750
So they'll be there with us?

119
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:25,290
Someone will guide you.

120
00:03:25,290 --> 00:03:26,430
Yeah, someone will take you through.

121
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:30,040
Are they actual people?

122
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:31,830
Yes.

123
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:34,470
(Already scared)
I hope they don't take me away.

124
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:37,580
(The crew's
greatest finger-heart moments)

125
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:39,030
Strike a pose

126
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:40,350
to find your perfect match.

127
00:03:41,380 --> 00:03:43,140
(Swaying with Ning)

128
00:03:44,220 --> 00:03:45,060
(Nailed it)

129
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:48,740
(He sends a heart)

130
00:03:49,820 --> 00:03:51,060
(Draw a little heart for you)

131
00:03:52,340 --> 00:03:53,740
(Can't hold it in)

132
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:55,220
What's that supposed to mean?

133
00:03:55,260 --> 00:03:57,060
(Ding copies him)

134
00:03:57,080 --> 00:03:59,430
(Ning's roast mode: On)
You call yourself a singer-dancer?

135
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:01,030
You started out singing and dancing,

136
00:04:01,030 --> 00:04:01,540
Ke.

137
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:02,670
And that's all you've got?

138
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:04,390
(Ning shows how it's done)
Shouldn't you bust out a real move?

139
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:04,910
This one.

140
00:04:04,920 --> 00:04:06,270
(Ke explains)
There aren't any complicated moves.

141
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:06,670
Oh my God.

142
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:07,500
All right.

143
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:08,510
Isn't that 520?

144
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:09,430
(It clicks)
Is it?

145
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:10,230
It's 520.

146
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:10,630
Right.

147
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:12,390
Like this?

148
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:13,830
Yeah, 520!

149
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:15,590
This is the 20.

150
00:04:15,590 --> 00:04:16,940
(Starting to get it)
520.

151
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:18,270
(5 = me)
I'm over here.

152
00:04:18,280 --> 00:04:19,340
(2 (yeah) 0)
I'm 250.

153
00:04:19,340 --> 00:04:20,260
(Ke cracks a joke)

154
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:21,870
You're 502.

155
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:23,700
One more time, right?

156
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:25,500
(Ning is ready)
Yeah, let's go.

157
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:28,420
(Still swaying along with Ning)

158
00:04:29,780 --> 00:04:32,100
(A giant finger heart)

159
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:35,740
(Sending you a heart)

160
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:37,860
(Drawing a heart for you)

161
00:04:37,940 --> 00:04:39,780
(Ke-style finger heart)

162
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:40,470
Yours is kind of...

163
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:41,150
Ke.

164
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:43,150
A finger heart, Ke.

165
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:44,950
That's from the Leaning Sway.

166
00:04:44,950 --> 00:04:45,230
Yeah.

167
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,550
The second I saw yours, I changed mine.

168
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:47,600
You saw me switch moves, right?

169
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:48,060
I changed it to this.

170
00:04:48,090 --> 00:04:49,260
You changed it to that.

171
00:04:49,260 --> 00:04:51,420
(The crew tries face-swapping)

172
00:04:51,460 --> 00:04:52,540
(Waiting for setup)

173
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:54,150
Yeah, swap my face with Liu Yuning's.

174
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:55,390
Say something he'd say.

175
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:55,990
Do an impression.

176
00:04:56,440 --> 00:04:57,400
(For example...)
I'd probably say,

177
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,350
for example...

178
00:04:58,350 --> 00:04:59,500
Just as an example.

179
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:00,910
Just as an example.

180
00:05:02,820 --> 00:05:03,540
(Try it upside down?)

181
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:04,870
This actually looks pretty good.

182
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:06,020
It's all blurry.

183
00:05:06,020 --> 00:05:06,540
(Too busy admiring the beauty)

184
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:09,060
It has that old-school camcorder vibe.

185
00:05:09,060 --> 00:05:09,900
(A meeting of camera minds)

186
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:11,270
It's fine.

187
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:13,660
If it's upside down,
just leave it like that.

188
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:14,220
(Photographer He on duty)

189
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:17,670
For example.

190
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:20,260
Oh, we were holding it upside down.

191
00:05:20,260 --> 00:05:21,580
(Finally figured it out)

192
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:22,870
Let me try.

193
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:23,910
I'll try another guy.

194
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:24,870
Try another guy.

195
00:05:24,880 --> 00:05:25,990
Yeah, pick another guy.

196
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:32,310
It kind of...

197
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:33,230
This...

198
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:35,830
Looks like a childhood photo of you.

199
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:36,470
No, try...

200
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:37,230
someone else.

201
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:38,070
I mean, switch

202
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:38,980
to another person.

203
00:05:38,980 --> 00:05:40,220
(Here we go)

204
00:05:40,240 --> 00:05:40,710
They all look the same.

205
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:42,740
Try Zhang Linghe. Let's see.

206
00:05:43,350 --> 00:05:44,580
Yeah, try Zhang Linghe.

207
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:48,670
Guys...

208
00:05:48,860 --> 00:05:50,180
(Laughing out of frame)

209
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:51,270
Guys, this is...

210
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:54,470
I think this face-swap app
is kind of broken.

211
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:55,830
(Here's your "He")
Is this right?

212
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:57,390
This is... This...

213
00:05:57,400 --> 00:05:59,590
It still looks like you.

214
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:00,990
Still looks like Ding.

215
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,430
Let me try. Come on.

216
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:03,910
That's my face, right?

217
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:06,960
This one kind of looks like him.

218
00:06:07,390 --> 00:06:08,730
Yeah, kind of.

219
00:06:08,730 --> 00:06:10,100
This one really does.

220
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:15,960
I'll...

221
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:16,510
I'll swap myself with myself.

222
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:17,630
Swap yourself with yourself?

223
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:18,670
That's weird.

224
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:20,190
Swap yourself with yourself,

225
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:21,310
and it should just look like you.

226
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:22,750
It doesn't look like you at all.

227
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:24,460
(Like a totally different person)

228
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,670
Swapping your own face onto yourself

229
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:26,670
doesn't look like you at all.

230
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:28,150
Oh no, not even close.

231
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:29,510
Oh, I get it now.

232
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:30,590
I get it.

233
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:32,070
Let's try.

234
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:32,870
Who else?

235
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:34,430
Then let's try Qian...

236
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:35,830
Qian Jinding.

237
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:38,350
Oh my God.

238
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:41,750
Oh my gosh.

239
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:42,670
Does this even work?

240
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:44,270
Is this right?

241
00:06:44,280 --> 00:06:45,390
Do we need to wipe the lens?

242
00:06:45,400 --> 00:06:47,110
Hold on, let me clean it.

243
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:49,510
Maybe it's just too dark in here.

244
00:06:49,520 --> 00:06:50,070
Yeah.

245
00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:53,420
(Whatever the job, they nail it)

246
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:55,760
She's mine!

247
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:56,230
What are you looking at?

248
00:06:56,230 --> 00:06:57,780
She's mine!

249
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:00,760
What's this?

250
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:01,530
This is the showcase

251
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:03,870
of work by our Employee of the Day.

252
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:10,460
Those legs...

253
00:07:10,460 --> 00:07:17,060
(Employee of the Day showcase)

254
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:18,550
That dancing is actually really good.

255
00:07:23,780 --> 00:07:25,700
(Perfectly in sync)

256
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:27,430
You guys have real stage presence.

257
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:32,710
Nice.

258
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:35,030
She's mine!

259
00:07:35,030 --> 00:07:35,590
Back off!

260
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:36,430
What?

261
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:37,590
She's mine!

262
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:41,550
What are you guys talking about?

263
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:42,150
She's mine!

264
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:44,670
Stop fighting, you guys.

265
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:45,750
She's mine!

266
00:07:46,640 --> 00:07:47,600
Back off!

267
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:48,570
She's mine!

268
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:50,830
Mine. She's mine!

269
00:07:50,830 --> 00:07:51,510
Mine.

270
00:07:51,510 --> 00:07:52,180
You're mine!

271
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:52,680
Mine.

272
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:53,250
You're mine!

273
00:07:53,250 --> 00:07:54,010
No, she's mine!

274
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:56,030
See? We can

275
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:57,590
succeed at anything we do.

276
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:58,510
(Talent always shines)
Seriously.

277
00:07:58,520 --> 00:07:59,470
Whatever the job, we nail it.

278
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,820
We're this good,
and we don't get snacks?

279
00:08:02,820 --> 00:08:03,780
(Still only thinking about food)

280
00:08:06,100 --> 00:08:06,940
=The Truth (Season 4)=

281
00:08:06,950 --> 00:08:08,070
(SVIP updates Wed & Thu at noon.)

282
